13.1.4.8 FormData
.................

A *note FormData: a8. object contains the form data and also handles
encoding it into a body that is either ‘multipart/form-data’ or
‘application/x-www-form-urlencoded’.  ‘multipart/form-data’ is used if
at least one field is an io.IOBase(1) object or was added with at least
one optional argument to *note add_field: 125. (‘content_type’,
‘filename’, or ‘content_transfer_encoding’).  Otherwise,
‘application/x-www-form-urlencoded’ is used.

*note FormData: a8. instances are callable and return a
‘aiohttp.payload.Payload’ on being called.

 -- Class: aiohttp.FormData (fields, quote_fields=True, charset=None)

     Helper class for multipart/form-data and
     application/x-www-form-urlencoded body generation.


     Parameters: ‘fields’ – A container for the key/value pairs of this
     form.

     Possible types are:

        - dict(2)

        - tuple(3) or list(4)

        - io.IOBase(5), e.g.  a file-like object

        - multidict.MultiDict(6) or multidict.MultiDictProxy(7)

     If it is a tuple(8) or list(9), it must be a valid argument for
     *note add_fields: 126.

     For dict(10), multidict.MultiDict(11), and
     multidict.MultiDictProxy(12), the keys and values must be valid
     ‘name’ and ‘value’ arguments to *note add_field: 125, respectively.

      -- Method: add_field (name, value, content_type=None,
               filename=None, content_transfer_encoding=None)

          Add a field to the form.


          Parameters:

             * ‘name’ (str(13)) – Name of the field

             * ‘value’ – Value of the field

               Possible types are:

                  - str(14)

                  - bytes(15), bytearray(16), or memoryview(17)

                  - io.IOBase(18), e.g.  a file-like object

             * ‘content_type’ (str(19)) – The field’s content-type
               header (optional)

             * ‘filename’ (str(20)) – The field’s filename (optional)

               If this is not set and ‘value’ is a bytes(21),
               bytearray(22), or memoryview(23) object, the ‘name’
               argument is used as the filename unless
               ‘content_transfer_encoding’ is specified.

               If ‘filename’ is not set and ‘value’ is an io.IOBase(24)
               object, the filename is extracted from the object if
               possible.

             * ‘content_transfer_encoding’ (str(25)) – The field’s
               content-transfer-encoding header (optional)

      -- Method: add_fields (fields)

          Add one or more fields to the form.


          Parameters: ‘fields’ – An iterable containing:

             - io.IOBase(26), e.g.  a file-like object

             - multidict.MultiDict(27) or multidict.MultiDictProxy(28)

             - tuple(29) or list(30) of length two, containing a
               name-value pair

