 -- Class: aiohttp.TraceConfig
          (trace_config_ctx_factory=SimpleNamespace)

     Trace config is the configuration object used to trace requests
     launched by a *note ClientSession: 2e. object using different
     events related to different parts of the request flow.


     Parameters: ‘trace_config_ctx_factory’ – factory used to create
     trace contexts, default class used types.SimpleNamespace(1)

      -- Method: trace_config_ctx (trace_request_ctx=None)


          Parameters: ‘trace_request_ctx’ – Will be used to pass as a kw
          for the ‘trace_config_ctx_factory’.

          Build a new trace context from the config.

     Every signal handler should have the following signature:

          async def on_signal(session, context, params): ...

     where ‘session’ is *note ClientSession: 2e. instance, ‘context’ is
     an object returned by *note trace_config_ctx(): 152. call and
     ‘params’ is a data class with signal parameters.  The type of
     ‘params’ depends on subscribed signal and described below.

