13.2.2.9 Reading from the same task in WebSockets
.................................................

Reading from the 'WebSocket' (‘await ws.receive()’) 'must only' be done
inside the request handler 'task'; however, writing (‘ws.send_str(...)’)
to the 'WebSocket', closing (‘await ws.close()’) and canceling the
handler task may be delegated to other tasks.  See also *note FAQ
section: 1ed.

*note aiohttp.web: 3. creates an implicit asyncio.Task(1) for handling
every incoming request.

     Note: While *note aiohttp.web: 3. itself only supports 'WebSockets'
     without downgrading to 'LONG-POLLING', etc., our team supports
     SockJS(2), an aiohttp-based library for implementing
     SockJS-compatible server code.

     Warning: Parallel reads from websocket are forbidden, there is no
     possibility to call *note WebSocketResponse.receive(): 1ee. from
     two tasks.

     See *note FAQ section: 1ef. for instructions how to solve the
     problem.

   ---------- Footnotes ----------

   (1) https://docs.python.org/3/library/asyncio-task.html#asyncio.Task

   (2) https://github.com/aio-libs/sockjs


