* Menu:

* Abstract::
* Run a Basic Low-Level Server::


File: aiohttp.info,  Node: Abstract,  Next: Run a Basic Low-Level Server,  Up: Low Level Server

13.2.3.1 Abstract
.................

Sometimes user don’t need high-level concepts introduced in *note
Server: a.: applications, routers, middlewares and signals.

All what is needed is supporting asynchronous callable which accepts a
request and returns a response object.

This is done by introducing *note aiohttp.web.Server: 234. class which
serves a 'protocol factory' role for asyncio.loop.create_server()(1) and
bridges data stream to 'web handler' and sends result back.

Low level 'web handler' should accept the single *note BaseRequest: 235.
parameter and performs one of the following actions:

       1. Return a *note Response: 19c. with the whole HTTP body stored
          in memory.

       2. Create a *note StreamResponse: 1a5, send headers by *note
          StreamResponse.prepare(): 20a. call, send data chunks by *note
          StreamResponse.write(): 236. and return finished response.

       3. Raise *note HTTPException: 1d8. derived exception (see *note
          Exceptions: 1d6. section).

          All other exceptions not derived from *note HTTPException:
          1d8. leads to '500 Internal Server Error' response.

       4. Initiate and process Web-Socket connection by *note
          WebSocketResponse: 1d3. using (see *note WebSockets: b.).

   ---------- Footnotes ----------

   (1) 
https://docs.python.org/3/library/asyncio-eventloop.html#asyncio.loop.create_server


