....................

Access logs are enabled by default.  If the ‘debug’ flag is set, and the
default logger ‘'aiohttp.access'’ is used, access logs will be output to
stderr(1) if no handlers are attached.  Furthermore, if the default
logger has no log level set, the log level will be set to
logging.DEBUG(2).

This logging may be controlled by *note aiohttp.web.AppRunner(): 215.
and *note aiohttp.web.run_app(): 19e.

To override the default logger, pass an instance of logging.Logger(3) to
override the default logger.

     Note: Use ‘web.run_app(app, access_log=None)’ to disable access
     logs.

In addition, 'access_log_format' may be used to specify the log format.

