13.2.7.6 Nginx+Gunicorn
.......................

aiohttp can be deployed using Gunicorn(1), which is based on a pre-fork
worker model.  Gunicorn launches your app as worker processes for
handling incoming requests.

As opposed to deployment with *note bare Nginx: 362, this solution does
not need to manually run several aiohttp processes and use a tool like
supervisord to monitor them.  But nothing is free: running aiohttp
application under gunicorn is slightly slower.

