13.3.4.3 Helpers
................

 -- Method: StreamReader.exception ()

     Get the exception occurred on data reading.

 -- Method: aiohttp.is_eof ()

     Return ‘True’ if EOF was reached.

     Internal buffer may be not empty at the moment.

     See also
     ........

     *note StreamReader.at_eof(): 3c5.

 -- Method: StreamReader.at_eof ()

     Return ‘True’ if the buffer is empty and EOF was reached.

 -- Method: StreamReader.read_nowait (n=None)

     Returns data from internal buffer if any, empty bytes object
     otherwise.

     Raises RuntimeError(1) if other coroutine is waiting for stream.


     Parameters: ‘n’ (int(2)) – how many bytes to read, ‘-1’ for the
     whole internal buffer.


     Return bytes: the given data

 -- Method: StreamReader.unread_data (data)

     Rollback reading some data from stream, inserting it to buffer
     head.


     Parameters: ‘data’ (bytes(3)) – data to push back into the stream.

          Warning: The method does not wake up waiters.

          E.g.  *note read(): 3b7. will not be resumed.

 -- Method: aiohttp.wait_eof ()

 -- Method: :async:

     Wait for EOF. The given data may be accessible by upcoming read
     calls.

