13.4.3 How do I create a route that matches urls with a given prefix?
---------------------------------------------------------------------

You can do something like the following:

     app.router.add_route('*', '/path/to/{tail:.+}', sink_handler)

The first argument, ‘*’, matches any HTTP method ('GET, POST, OPTIONS',
etc).  The second argument matches URLS with the desired prefix.  The
third argument is the handler function.


