13.4.5 How can middleware store data for web handlers to use?
-------------------------------------------------------------

Both *note aiohttp.web.Request: 19b. and *note aiohttp.web.Application:
19d. support the dict(1) interface.

Therefore, data may be stored inside a request object.

     async def handler(request):
         request['unique_key'] = data

See ‘https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp_session’ code for an example.
The ‘aiohttp_session.get_session(request)’ method uses ‘SESSION_KEY’ for
saving request-specific session information.

As of aiohttp 3.0, all response objects are dict-like structures as
well.

   ---------- Footnotes ----------

   (1) https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#dict


