13.5.3.45 Bug fixes
...................

   - Fixed cookie parsing to be more lenient when handling cookies with
     special characters in names or values.  Cookies with characters
     like ‘{’, ‘}’, and ‘/’ in names are now accepted instead of causing
     a CookieError(1) and 500 errors.  Additionally, cookies with
     mismatched quotes in values are now parsed correctly, and quoted
     cookie values are now handled consistently whether or not they
     include special attributes like ‘Domain’.  Also fixed *note
     CookieJar: 63. to ensure shared cookies (domain=””, path=””)
     respect the ‘quote_cookie’ parameter, making cookie quoting
     behavior consistent for all cookies – by @bdraco(2).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #2683(3), #5397(4),
     #7993(5), #11112(6).

   - Fixed an issue where cookies with duplicate names but different
     domains or paths were lost when updating the cookie jar.  The *note
     ClientSession: 2e. cookie jar now correctly stores all cookies even
     if they have the same name but different domain or path, following
     the RFC 6265 Section 5.3(7) storage model – by @bdraco(8).

     Note that *note ClientResponse.cookies: d3. returns a
     SimpleCookie(9) which uses the cookie name as a key, so only the
     last cookie with each name is accessible via this interface.  All
     cookies can be accessed via
     ClientResponse.headers.getall('Set-Cookie')(10) if needed.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #4486(11),
     #11105(12), #11106(13).

