13.5.3.59 Features
..................

   - Added support for reusable request bodies to enable retries,
     redirects, and digest authentication – by @bdraco(1) and
     @GLGDLY(2).

     Most payloads can now be safely reused multiple times, fixing
     long-standing issues where POST requests with form data or file
     uploads would fail on redirects with errors like “Form data has
     been processed already” or “I/O operation on closed file”.  This
     also enables digest authentication to work with request bodies and
     allows retry mechanisms to resend requests without consuming the
     payload.  Note that payloads derived from async iterables may still
     not be reusable in some cases.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #5530(3), #5577(4),
     #9201(5), #11017(6).

