13.5.3.120 Bug fixes
....................

   - Raise *note aiohttp.ServerFingerprintMismatch: 144. exception on
     client-side if request through http proxy with mismatching server
     fingerprint digest: ‘aiohttp.ClientSession(headers=headers,
     connector=TCPConnector(ssl=aiohttp.Fingerprint(mismatch_digest),
     trust_env=True).request(…)’ – by @gangj(1).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6652(2).

   - Modified websocket *note
     aiohttp.ClientWebSocketResponse.receive_str(): f5, *note
     aiohttp.ClientWebSocketResponse.receive_bytes(): f7, *note
     aiohttp.web.WebSocketResponse.receive_str(): 28d. & *note
     aiohttp.web.WebSocketResponse.receive_bytes(): 28e. methods to
     raise new *note aiohttp.WSMessageTypeError: f6. exception, instead
     of generic TypeError(3), when websocket messages of incorrect types
     are received – by @ara-25(4).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6800(5).

   - Made ‘TestClient.app’ a ‘Generic’ so type checkers will know the
     correct type (avoiding unneeded ‘client.app is not None’ checks) –
     by @Dreamsorcerer(6).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8977(7).

   - Fixed the keep-alive connection pool to be FIFO instead of LIFO –
     by @bdraco(8).

