13.5.3.121 Features
...................

   - Added ‘strategy’ parameter to *note
     aiohttp.web.StreamResponse.enable_compression(): 26c. The value of
     this parameter is passed to the zlib.compressobj()(1) function,
     allowing people to use a more sufficient compression algorithm for
     their data served by *note aiohttp.web: 3. – by @shootkin(2)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6257(3).

   - Added ‘server_hostname’ parameter to ‘ws_connect’.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #7941(4).

   - Exported *note ClientWSTimeout: b0. to top-level namespace – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(5).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8612(6).

   - Added ‘secure’/‘httponly’/‘samesite’ parameters to ‘.del_cookie()’
     – by @Dreamsorcerer(7).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8956(8).

   - Updated *note ClientSession: 2e.’s auth logic to include default
     auth only if the request URL’s origin matches _base_url; otherwise,
     the auth will not be included – by @MaximZemskov(9)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8966(10), #9466(11).

   - Added ‘proxy’ and ‘proxy_auth’ parameters to *note ClientSession:
     2e. – by @meshya(12).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9207(13).

   - Added ‘default_to_multipart’ parameter to ‘FormData’.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9335(14).

   - Added *note send_frame(): f0. and *note send_frame(): 281. for
     WebSockets – by @bdraco(15).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9348(16).

   - Updated *note ClientSession: 2e. to support paths in ‘base_url’
     parameter.  ‘base_url’ paths must end with a ‘/’ – by
     @Cycloctane(17).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9530(18).

   - Improved performance of reading WebSocket messages with a Cython
     implementation – by @bdraco(19).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9543(20), #9554(21),
     #9556(22), #9558(23), #9636(24), #9649(25), #9781(26).

   - Added ‘writer_limit’ to the *note WebSocketResponse: 1d3. to be
     able to adjust the limit before the writer forces the buffer to be
     drained – by @bdraco(27).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9572(28).

   - Added an *note enabled: 382. property to *note
     aiohttp.abc.AbstractAccessLogger: 29b. to dynamically check if
     logging is enabled – by @bdraco(29).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9822(30).

