13.5.3.145 Bug fixes
....................

   - Added *note aiohttp.ClientConnectionResetError: 13b.  Client code
     that previously threw ConnectionResetError(1) will now throw this –
     by @Dreamsorcerer(2).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9137(3).

   - Fixed an unclosed transport ‘ResourceWarning’ on web handlers – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(4).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8875(5).

   - Fixed resolve_host() ‘Task was destroyed but is pending’ errors –
     by @Dreamsorcerer(6).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8967(7).

   - Fixed handling of some file-like objects (e.g.
     ‘tarfile.extractfile()’) which raise ‘AttributeError’ instead of
     ‘OSError’ when ‘fileno’ fails for streaming payload data – by
     @ReallyReivax(8).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6732(9).

   - Fixed web router not matching pre-encoded URLs (requires yarl
     1.9.6+) – by @Dreamsorcerer(10).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8898(11), #9267(12).

   - Fixed an error when trying to add a route for multiple methods with
     a path containing a regex pattern – by @Dreamsorcerer(13).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8998(14).

   - Fixed ‘Response.text’ when body is a ‘Payload’ – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(15).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6485(16).

   - Fixed compressed requests failing when no body was provided – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(17).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9108(18).

   - Fixed client incorrectly reusing a connection when the previous
     message had not been fully sent – by @Dreamsorcerer(19).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8992(20).

   - Fixed race condition that could cause server to close connection
     incorrectly at keepalive timeout – by @Dreamsorcerer(21).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9140(22).

   - Fixed Python parser chunked handling with multiple
     Transfer-Encoding values – by @Dreamsorcerer(23).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8823(24).

   - Fixed error handling after 100-continue so server sends 500
     response instead of disconnecting – by @Dreamsorcerer(25).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8876(26).

   - Stopped adding a default Content-Type header when response has no
     content – by @Dreamsorcerer(27).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8858(28).

   - Added support for URL credentials with empty (zero-length)
     username, e.g.  ‘https://:password@host’ – by @shuckc(29)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6494(30).

   - Stopped logging exceptions from ‘web.run_app()’ that would be
     raised regardless – by @Dreamsorcerer(31).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #6807(32).

   - Implemented binding to IPv6 addresses in the pytest server fixture.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #4650(33).

   - Fixed the incorrect use of flags for ‘getnameinfo()’ in the
     Resolver –by @GitNMLee(34)

     Link-Local IPv6 addresses can now be handled by the Resolver
     correctly.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9032(35).

   - Fixed StreamResponse.prepared to return True after EOF is sent – by
     @arthurdarcet(36).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #5343(37).

   - Changed ‘make_mocked_request()’ to use empty payload by default –
     by @rahulnht(38).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #7167(39).

   - Used more precise type for ‘ClientResponseError.headers’, fixing
     some type errors when using them – by @Dreamsorcerer(40).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8768(41).

   - Changed behavior when returning an invalid response to send a 500
     response – by @Dreamsorcerer(42).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8845(43).

   - Fixed response reading from closed session to throw an error
     immediately instead of timing out – by @Dreamsorcerer(44).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8878(45).

   - Fixed ‘CancelledError’ from one cleanup context stopping other
     contexts from completing – by @Dreamsorcerer(46).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8908(47).

   - Fixed changing scheme/host in ‘Response.clone()’ for absolute URLs
     – by @Dreamsorcerer(48).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8990(49).

   - Fixed ‘Site.name’ when host is an empty string – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(50).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8929(51).

   - Updated Python parser to reject messages after a close message,
     matching C parser behaviour – by @Dreamsorcerer(52).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9018(53).

   - Fixed creation of ‘SSLContext’ inside of *note
     aiohttp.TCPConnector: 73. with multiple event loops in different
     threads – by @bdraco(54).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9029(55).

   - Fixed (on Python 3.11+) some edge cases where a task cancellation
     may get incorrectly suppressed – by @Dreamsorcerer(56).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9030(57).

   - Fixed exception information getting lost on ‘HttpProcessingError’ –
     by @Dreamsorcerer(58).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9052(59).

   - Fixed ‘If-None-Match’ not using weak comparison – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(60).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9063(61).

   - Fixed badly encoded charset crashing when getting response text
     instead of falling back to charset detector.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9160(62).

   - Rejected ‘n’ in ‘reason’ values to avoid sending broken HTTP
     messages – by @Dreamsorcerer(63).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9167(64).

   - Changed *note ClientResponse.raise_for_status(): 97. to only
     release the connection when invoked outside an ‘async with’ context
     – by @Dreamsorcerer(65).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #9239(66).

