13.5.3.172 Removals and backward incompatible breaking changes
..............................................................

   - The shutdown logic in 3.9 waited on all tasks, which caused issues
     with some libraries.  In 3.10 we’ve changed this logic to only wait
     on request handlers.  This means that it’s important for developers
     to correctly handle the lifecycle of background tasks using a
     library such as ‘aiojobs’.  If an application is using
     ‘handler_cancellation=True’ then it is also a good idea to ensure
     that any asyncio.shield()(1) calls are replaced with
     aiojobs.aiohttp.shield()(2).

     Please read the updated documentation on these points:
     ‘https://docs.aiohttp.org/en/stable/web_advanced.html#graceful-shutdown’
     ‘https://docs.aiohttp.org/en/stable/web_advanced.html#web-handler-cancellation’

     – by @Dreamsorcerer(3)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8495(4).

   ---------- Footnotes ----------

   (1) 
https://docs.python.org/3/library/asyncio-task.html#asyncio.shield

   (2) 
https://aiojobs.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api.html#aiojobs.aiohttp.shield

   (3) https://github.com/sponsors/Dreamsorcerer

   (4) https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/8495


