13.5.3.175 Miscellaneous internal changes
.........................................

   - Improved URL handler resolution time by indexing resources in the
     UrlDispatcher.  For applications with a large number of handlers,
     this should increase performance significantly.  – by @bdraco(1)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #7829(2).

   - Added nacl_middleware(3) to the list of middlewares in the third
     party section of the documentation.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8346(4).

   - Minor improvements to static typing – by @Dreamsorcerer(5).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8364(6).

   - Added a 3.11-specific overloads to ‘ClientSession’ – by
     @max-muoto(7).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8463(8).

   - Simplified path checks for ‘UrlDispatcher.add_static()’ method – by
     @steverep(9).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8491(10).

   - Avoided creating a future on every websocket receive – by
     @bdraco(11).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8498(12).

   - Updated identity checks for all ‘WSMsgType’ type compares – by
     @bdraco(13).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8501(14).

   - When using Python 3.12 or later, the writer is no longer scheduled
     on the event loop if it can finish synchronously.  Avoiding event
     loop scheduling reduces latency and improves performance.  – by
     @bdraco(15).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8510(16).

   - Restored ‘AsyncResolver’ to be the default resolver.  – by
     @bdraco(17).

     ‘AsyncResolver’ was disabled by default because of IPv6
     compatibility issues.  These issues have been resolved and
     ‘AsyncResolver’ is again now the default resolver.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8522(18).

