13.5.3.179 Bug fixes
....................

   - The asynchronous internals now set the underlying causes when
     assigning exceptions to the future objects – by @webknjaz(1).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8089(2).

   - Treated values of ‘Accept-Encoding’ header as case-insensitive when
     checking for gzip files – by @steverep(3).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8104(4).

   - Improved the DNS resolution performance on cache hit – by
     @bdraco(5).

     This is achieved by avoiding an asyncio(6) task creation in this
     case.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8163(7).

   - Changed the type annotations to allow ‘dict’ on *note
     aiohttp.MultipartWriter.append(): 39a, *note
     aiohttp.MultipartWriter.append_json(): 39b. and *note
     aiohttp.MultipartWriter.append_form(): 39c. – by @cakemanny(8)

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #7741(9).

   - Ensure websocket transport is closed when client does not close it
     – by @bdraco(10).

     The transport could remain open if the client did not close it.
     This change ensures the transport is closed when the client does
     not close it.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8200(11).

   - Leave websocket transport open if receive times out or is cancelled
     – by @bdraco(12).

     This restores the behavior prior to the change in #7978.

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8251(13).

   - Fixed content not being read when an upgrade request was not
     supported with the pure Python implementation.  – by @bdraco(14).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8252(15).

   - Fixed a race condition with incoming connections during server
     shutdown – by @Dreamsorcerer(16).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8271(17).

   - Fixed ‘multipart/form-data’ compliance with RFC 7578(18) – by
     @Dreamsorcerer(19).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8280(20).

   - Fixed blocking I/O in the event loop while processing files in a
     POST request – by @bdraco(21).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8283(22).

   - Escaped filenames in static view – by @bdraco(23).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8317(24).

   - Fixed the pure python parser to mark a connection as closing when a
     response has no length – by @Dreamsorcerer(25).

     'Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:' #8320(26).

