13.5.3.200 Bugfixes
...................

   - Implemented stripping the trailing dots from fully-qualified domain
     names in ‘Host’ headers and TLS context when acting as an HTTP
     client.  This allows the client to connect to URLs with FQDN host
     name like ‘https://example.com./’.  – by @martin-sucha(1).

     #3636(2)

   - Fixed client timeout not working when incoming data is always
     available without waiting.  – by @Dreamsorcerer(3).

     #5854(4)

   - Fixed ‘readuntil’ to work with a delimiter of more than one
     character.

     #6701(5)

   - Added ‘__repr__’ to ‘EmptyStreamReader’ to avoid ‘AttributeError’.

     #6916(6)

   - Fixed bug when using ‘TCPConnector’ with ‘ttl_dns_cache=0’.

     #7014(7)

   - Fixed response returned from expect handler being thrown away.  –
     by @Dreamsorcerer(8)

     #7025(9)

   - Avoided raising ‘UnicodeDecodeError’ in multipart and in HTTP
     headers parsing.

     #7044(10)

   - Changed ‘sock_read’ timeout to start after writing has finished,
     avoiding read timeouts caused by an unfinished write.  – by
     @dtrifiro(11)

     #7149(12)

   - Fixed missing query in tracing method URLs when using ‘yarl’ 1.9+.

     #7259(13)

   - Changed max 32-bit timestamp to an aware datetime object, for
     consistency with the non-32-bit one, and to avoid a
     ‘DeprecationWarning’ on Python 3.12.

     #7302(14)

   - Fixed ‘EmptyStreamReader.iter_chunks()’ never ending.  – by
     @mind1m(15)

     #7616(16)

   - Fixed a rare ‘RuntimeError: await wasn't used with future’
     exception.  – by @stalkerg(17)

     #7785(18)

   - Fixed issue with insufficient HTTP method and version validation.

     #7700(19)

   - Added check to validate that absolute URIs have schemes.

     #7712(20)

   - Fixed unhandled exception when Python HTTP parser encounters
     unpaired Unicode surrogates.

     #7715(21)

   - Updated parser to disallow invalid characters in header field names
     and stop accepting LF as a request line separator.

     #7719(22)

   - Fixed Python HTTP parser not treating 204/304/1xx as an empty body.

     #7755(23)

   - Ensure empty body response for 1xx/204/304 per RFC 9112 sec 6.3.

     #7756(24)

   - Fixed an issue when a client request is closed before completing a
     chunked payload.  – by @Dreamsorcerer(25)

     #7764(26)

   - Edge Case Handling for ResponseParser for missing reason value.

     #7776(27)

   - Fixed ‘ClientWebSocketResponse.close_code’ being erroneously set to
     ‘None’ when there are concurrent async tasks receiving data and
     closing the connection.

     #7306(28)

   - Added HTTP method validation.

     #6533(29)

   - Fixed arbitrary sequence types being allowed to inject values via
     version parameter.  – by @Dreamsorcerer(30)

     #7835(31)

   - Performance: Fixed increase in latency with small messages from
     websocket compression changes.

     #7797(32)

