13.5.3.228 Bugfixes
...................

   - Modify _drain_helper() to handle concurrent ‘await resp.write(…)’
     or ‘ws.send_json(…)’ calls without race-condition.  #2934(1)

   - Started using ‘MultiLoopChildWatcher’ when it’s available under
     POSIX while setting up the test I/O loop.  #3450(2)

   - Only encode content-disposition filename parameter using
     percent-encoding.  Other parameters are encoded to quoted-string or
     RFC2231 extended parameter value.  #4012(3)

   - Fixed HTTP client requests to honor ‘no_proxy’ environment
     variables.  #4431(4)

   - Fix supporting WebSockets proxies configured via environment
     variables.  #4648(5)

   - Change return type on URLDispatcher to UrlMappingMatchInfo to
     improve type annotations.  #4748(6)

   - Ensure a cleanup context is cleaned up even when an exception
     occurs during startup.  #4799(7)

   - Added a new exception type for Unix socket client errors which
     provides a more useful error message.  #4984(8)

   - Remove Transfer-Encoding and Content-Type headers for 204 in
     StreamResponse #5106(9)

   - Only depend on typing_extensions for Python <3.8 #5107(10)

   - Add ABNORMAL_CLOSURE and BAD_GATEWAY to WSCloseCode #5192(11)

   - Fix cookies disappearing from HTTPExceptions.  #5233(12)

   - StaticResource prefixes no longer match URLs with a non-folder
     prefix.  For example ‘routes.static('/foo', '/foo')’ no longer
     matches the URL ‘/foobar’.  Previously, this would attempt to load
     the file ‘/foo/ar’.  #5250(13)

   - Acquire the connection before running traces to prevent race
     condition.  #5259(14)

   - Add missing slots to ‘`_RequestContextManager’ and
     ‘_WSRequestContextManager’ #5329(15)

   - Ensure sending a zero byte file does not throw an exception (round
     2) #5380(16)

   - Set “text/plain” when data is an empty string in client requests.
     #5392(17)

   - Stop automatically releasing the ‘ClientResponse’ object on calls
     to the ‘ok’ property for the failed requests.  #5403(18)

   - Include query parameters from ‘params’ keyword argument in tracing
     ‘URL’. #5432(19)

   - Fix annotations #5466(20)

   - Fixed the multipart POST requests processing to always release file
     descriptors for the ‘tempfile.Temporaryfile’-created
     ‘_io.BufferedRandom’ instances of files sent within multipart
     request bodies via HTTP POST requests – by @webknjaz(21).
     #5494(22)

   - Fix 0 being incorrectly treated as an immediate timeout.  #5527(23)

   - Fixes failing tests when an environment variable <scheme>_proxy is
     set.  #5554(24)

   - Replace deprecated app handler design in ‘tests/autobahn/server.py’
     with call to ‘web.run_app’; replace deprecated ‘aiohttp.ws_connect’
     calls in ‘tests/autobahn/client.py’ with
     ‘aiohttp.ClienSession.ws_connect’.  #5606(25)

   - Fixed test for ‘HTTPUnauthorized’ that access the ‘text’ argument.
     This is not used in any part of the code, so it’s removed now.
     #5657(26)

   - Remove incorrect default from docs #5727(27)

   - Remove external test dependency to ‘http://httpbin.org’ #5840(28)

   - Don’t cancel current task when entering a cancelled timer.
     #5853(29)

   - Added ‘params’ keyword argument to ‘ClientSession.ws_connect’.  –
     @hoh(30).  #5868(31)

   - Uses ‘asyncio.ThreadedChildWatcher’ under POSIX to allow setting up
     test loop in non-main thread.  #5877(32)

   - Fix the error in handling the return value of ‘getaddrinfo’.
     ‘getaddrinfo’ will return an ‘(int, bytes)’ tuple, if CPython could
     not handle the address family.  It will cause a index out of range
     error in aiohttp.  For example, if user compile CPython with
     ‘–disable-ipv6’ option but his system enable the ipv6.  #5901(33)

   - Removed the deprecated ‘loop’ argument from the
     ‘asyncio.sleep’/‘gather’ calls #5905(34)

   - Return ‘None’ from ‘request.if_modified_since’,
     ‘request.if_unmodified_since’, ‘request.if_range’ and
     ‘response.last_modified’ when corresponding http date headers are
     invalid.  #5925(35)

   - Fix resetting ‘SIGCHLD’ signals in Gunicorn aiohttp Worker to fix
     ‘subprocesses’ that capture output having an incorrect
     ‘returncode’.  #6130(36)

   - Raise ‘400: Content-Length can't be present with Transfer-Encoding’
     if both ‘Content-Length’ and ‘Transfer-Encoding’ are sent by peer
     by both C and Python implementations #6182(37)

