13.5.3.234 Bugfixes
...................

   - '(SECURITY BUG)' Started preventing open redirects in the
     ‘aiohttp.web.normalize_path_middleware’ middleware.  For more
     details, see
     ‘https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/security/advisories/GHSA-v6wp-4m6f-gcjg’.

     Thanks to Beast Glatisant(1) for finding the first instance of this
     issue and Jelmer Vernooĳ(2) for reporting and tracking it down in
     aiohttp.  #5497(3)

   - Fix interpretation difference of the pure-Python and the
     Cython-based HTTP parsers construct a ‘yarl.URL’ object for HTTP
     request-target.

     Before this fix, the Python parser would turn the URI’s
     absolute-path for ‘//some-path’ into ‘/’ while the Cython code
     preserved it as ‘//some-path’.  Now, both do the latter.  #5498(4)

