13.5.3.246 Bugfixes
...................

   - Fix keepalive connections not being closed in time #3296(1)

   - Fix failed websocket handshake leaving connection hanging.
     #3380(2)

   - Fix tasks cancellation order on exit.  The run_app task needs to be
     cancelled first for cleanup hooks to run with all tasks intact.
     #3805(3)

   - Don’t start heartbeat until _writer is set #4062(4)

   - Fix handling of multipart file uploads without a content type.
     #4089(5)

   - Preserve view handler function attributes across middlewares
     #4174(6)

   - Fix the string representation of ‘ServerDisconnectedError’.
     #4175(7)

   - Raising RuntimeError when trying to get encoding from not read body
     #4214(8)

   - Remove warning messages from noop.  #4282(9)

   - Raise ClientPayloadError if FormData re-processed.  #4345(10)

   - Fix a warning about unfinished task in ‘web_protocol.py’ #4408(11)

   - Fixed ‘deflate’ compression.  According to RFC 2616 now.  #4506(12)

   - Fixed OverflowError on platforms with 32-bit time_t #4515(13)

   - Fixed request.body_exists returns wrong value for methods without
     body.  #4528(14)

   - Fix connecting to link-local IPv6 addresses.  #4554(15)

   - Fix a problem with connection waiters that are never awaited.
     #4562(16)

   - Always make sure transport is not closing before reuse a
     connection.

     Reuse a protocol based on keepalive in headers is unreliable.  For
     example, uWSGI will not support keepalive even it serves a HTTP 1.1
     request, except explicitly configure uWSGI with a
     ‘--http-keepalive’ option.

     Servers designed like uWSGI could cause aiohttp intermittently
     raise a ConnectionResetException when the protocol poll runs out
     and some protocol is reused.  #4587(17)

   - Handle the last CRLF correctly even if it is received via separate
     TCP segment.  #4630(18)

   - Fix the register_resource function to validate route name before
     splitting it so that route name can include python keywords.
     #4691(19)

   - Improve typing annotations for ‘web.Request’,
     ‘aiohttp.ClientResponse’ and ‘multipart’ module.  #4736(20)

   - Fix resolver task is not awaited when connector is cancelled
     #4795(21)

   - Fix a bug “Aiohttp doesn’t return any error on invalid request
     methods” #4798(22)

   - Fix HEAD requests for static content.  #4809(23)

   - Fix incorrect size calculation for memoryview #4890(24)

   - Add HTTPMove to _all__.  #4897(25)

   - Fixed the type annotations in the ‘tracing’ module.  #4912(26)

   - Fix typing for multipart ‘__aiter__’.  #4931(27)

   - Fix for race condition on connections in BaseConnector that leads
     to exceeding the connection limit.  #4936(28)

   - Add forced UTF-8 encoding for ‘application/rdap+json’ responses.
     #4938(29)

   - Fix inconsistency between Python and C http request parsers in
     parsing pct-encoded URL. #4972(30)

   - Fix connection closing issue in HEAD request.  #5012(31)

   - Fix type hint on BaseRunner.addresses (from ‘List[str]’ to
     ‘List[Any]’) #5086(32)

   - Make ‘web.run_app()’ more responsive to Ctrl+C on Windows for
     Python < 3.8.  It slightly increases CPU load as a side effect.
     #5098(33)

