13.5.3.275 Features
...................

   - The library type annotations are checked in strict mode now.

   - Add support for setting cookies for individual request (#2387(1))

   - Application.add_domain implementation (#2809(2))

   - The default ‘app’ in the request returned by
     ‘test_utils.make_mocked_request’ can now have objects assigned to
     it and retrieved using the ‘[]’ operator.  (#3174(3))

   - Make ‘request.url’ accessible when transport is closed.  (#3177(4))

   - Add ‘zlib_executor_size’ argument to ‘Response’ constructor to
     allow compression to run in a background executor to avoid blocking
     the main thread and potentially triggering health check failures.
     (#3205(5))

   - Enable users to set ‘ClientTimeout’ in ‘aiohttp.request’ (#3213(6))

   - Don’t raise a warning if ‘NETRC’ environment variable is not set
     and ‘~/.netrc’ file doesn’t exist.  (#3267(7))

   - Add default logging handler to web.run_app If the
     ‘Application.debug`’ flag is set and the default logger
     ‘aiohttp.access’ is used, access logs will now be output using a
     'stderr' ‘StreamHandler’ if no handlers are attached.  Furthermore,
     if the default logger has no log level set, the log level will be
     set to ‘DEBUG’.  (#3324(8))

   - Add method argument to ‘session.ws_connect()’.  Sometimes server
     API requires a different HTTP method for WebSocket connection
     establishment.  For example, ‘Docker exec’ needs POST. (#3378(9))

   - Create a task per request handling.  (#3406(10))

