     ‘ping’ message.  (#1024(13)) (#777(14))

   - Remove ‘web.Application’ dependency from ‘web.UrlDispatcher’
     (#1510(15))

   - Accepting back-pressure from slow websocket clients (#1367(16))

   - Do not pause transport during set_parser stage (#1211(17))

   - Lingering close does not terminate before timeout (#1559(18))

   - ‘setsockopt’ may raise ‘OSError’ exception if socket is closed
     already (#1595(19))

   - Lots of CancelledError when requests are interrupted (#1565(20))

   - Allow users to specify what should happen to decoding errors when
     calling a responses ‘text()’ method (#1542(21))

   - Back port std module ‘http.cookies’ for python3.4.2 (#1566(22))

   - Maintain url’s fragment in client response (#1314(23))

   - Allow concurrently close WebSocket connection (#754(24))

   - Gzipped responses with empty body raises ContentEncodingError
     (#609(25))

   - Return 504 if request handle raises TimeoutError.

   - Refactor how we use keep-alive and close lingering timeouts.

   - Close response connection if we can not consume whole http message
     during client response release

   - Abort closed ssl client transports, broken servers can keep socket
     open un-limit time (#1568(26))

   - Log warning instead of ‘RuntimeError’ is websocket connection is
     closed.

   - Deprecated: ‘aiohttp.protocol.HttpPrefixParser’ will be removed in
