   - Websockets: Stop ‘async for’ iteration when connection is closed
     (#1144(18))

   - Ensure TestClient HTTP methods return a context manager (#1318(19))

   - Raise ‘ClientDisconnectedError’ to ‘FlowControlStreamReader’ read
     function if ‘ClientSession’ object is closed by client when reading
     data.  (#1323(20))

   - Document deployment without ‘Gunicorn’ (#1120(21))

   - Add deprecation warning for MD5 and SHA1 digests when used for
     fingerprint of site certs in TCPConnector.  (#1186(22))

   - Implement sub-applications (#1301(23))

   - Don’t inherit ‘web.Request’ from ‘dict’ but implement
     ‘MutableMapping’ protocol.

   - Implement frozen signals

   - Don’t inherit ‘web.Application’ from ‘dict’ but implement
     ‘MutableMapping’ protocol.

   - Support freezing for web applications

   - Accept access_log parameter in ‘web.run_app’, use ‘None’ to disable
     logging

   - Don’t flap ‘tcp_cork’ and ‘tcp_nodelay’ in regular request
     handling.  ‘tcp_nodelay’ is still enabled by default.

   - Improve performance of web server by removing premature computing
     of Content-Type if the value was set by ‘web.Response’ constructor.

     While the patch boosts speed of trivial ‘web.Response(text=’OK’,
     content_type=’text/plain)’ very well please don’t expect
     significant boost of your application – a couple DB requests and
     business logic is still the main bottleneck.

   - Boost performance by adding a custom time service (#1350(24))

   - Extend ‘ClientResponse’ with ‘content_type’ and ‘charset’
     properties like in ‘web.Request’.  (#1349(25))

   - Disable aiodns by default (#559(26))

   - Don’t flap ‘tcp_cork’ in client code, use TCP_NODELAY mode by
     default.

   - Implement ‘web.Request.clone()’ (#1361(27))

