13.5.3.376 1.0.0 (2016-09-16)
.............................

   - Change default size for client session’s connection pool from
     unlimited to 20 (#977(1))

   - Add IE support for cookie deletion.  (#994(2))

   - Remove deprecated ‘WebSocketResponse.wait_closed’ method (BACKWARD
     INCOMPATIBLE)

   - Remove deprecated ‘force’ parameter for ‘ClientResponse.close’
     method (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE)

   - Avoid using of mutable CIMultiDict kw param in make_mocked_request
     (#997(3))

   - Make WebSocketResponse.close a little bit faster by avoiding new
     task creating just for timeout measurement

   - Add ‘proxy’ and ‘proxy_auth’ params to ‘client.get()’ and family,
     deprecate ‘ProxyConnector’ (#998(4))

   - Add support for websocket send_json and receive_json, synchronize
     server and client API for websockets (#984(5))

   - Implement router shourtcuts for most useful HTTP methods, use
     ‘app.router.add_get()’, ‘app.router.add_post()’ etc.  instead of
     ‘app.router.add_route()’ (#986(6))

   - Support SSL connections for gunicorn worker (#1003(7))

   - Move obsolete examples to legacy folder

   - Switch to multidict 2.0 and title-cased strings (#1015(8))

   - ‘{FOO}e’ logger format is case-sensitive now

   - Fix logger report for unix socket 8e8469b

   - Rename aiohttp.websocket to aiohttp._ws_impl

   - Rename ‘aiohttp.MsgType’ to ‘aiohttp.WSMsgType’

   - Introduce ‘aiohttp.WSMessage’ officially

   - Rename Message -> WSMessage

   - Remove deprecated decode param from resp.read(decode=True)

   - Use 5min default client timeout (#1028(9))

   - Relax HTTP method validation in UrlDispatcher (#1037(10))

   - Pin minimal supported asyncio version to 3.4.2+ (‘loop.is_close()’
     should be present)

   - Remove aiohttp.websocket module (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) Please use
     high-level client and server approaches

   - Link header for 451 status code is mandatory

   - Fix test_client fixture to allow multiple clients per test
     (#1072(11))

   - make_mocked_request now accepts dict as headers (#1073(12))

   - Add Python 3.5.2/3.6+ compatibility patch for async generator
     protocol change (#1082(13))

   - Improvement test_client can accept instance object (#1083(14))

   - Simplify ServerHttpProtocol implementation (#1060(15))

   - Add a flag for optional showing directory index for static file
     handling (#921(16))

   - Define ‘web.Application.on_startup()’ signal handler (#1103(17))

   - Drop ChunkedParser and LinesParser (#1111(18))

   - Call ‘Application.startup’ in GunicornWebWorker (#1105(19))

   - Fix client handling hostnames with 63 bytes when a port is given in
     the url (#1044(20))

   - Implement proxy support for ClientSession.ws_connect (#1025(21))

   - Return named tuple from WebSocketResponse.can_prepare (#1016(22))

   - Fix access_log_format in ‘GunicornWebWorker’ (#1117(23))

   - Setup Content-Type to application/octet-stream by default
     (#1124(24))

   - Deprecate debug parameter from app.make_handler(), use
     ‘Application(debug=True)’ instead (#1121(25))

   - Remove fragment string in request path (#846(26))

   - Use aiodns.DNSResolver.gethostbyname() if available (#1136(27))

   - Fix static file sending on uvloop when sendfile is available
     (#1093(28))

   - Make prettier urls if query is empty dict (#1143(29))

   - Fix redirects for HEAD requests (#1147(30))

   - Default value for ‘StreamReader.read_nowait’ is -1 from now
     (#1150(31))

   - ‘aiohttp.StreamReader’ is not inherited from ‘asyncio.StreamReader’
     from now (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) (#1150(32))

   - Streams documentation added (#1150(33))

   - Add ‘multipart’ coroutine method for web Request object (#1067(34))

   - Publish ClientSession.loop property (#1149(35))

   - Fix static file with spaces (#1140(36))

   - Fix piling up asyncio loop by cookie expiration callbacks
     (#1061(37))

   - Drop ‘Timeout’ class for sake of ‘async_timeout’ external library.
     ‘aiohttp.Timeout’ is an alias for ‘async_timeout.timeout’

   - ‘use_dns_cache’ parameter of ‘aiohttp.TCPConnector’ is ‘True’ by
     default (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) (#1152(38))

   - ‘aiohttp.TCPConnector’ uses asynchronous DNS resolver if available
     by default (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) (#1152(39))

   - Conform to RFC3986 - do not include url fragments in client
     requests (#1174(40))

   - Drop ‘ClientSession.cookies’ (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) (#1173(41))

   - Refactor ‘AbstractCookieJar’ public API (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE)
     (#1173(42))

   - Fix clashing cookies with have the same name but belong to
     different domains (BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE) (#1125(43))

   - Support binary Content-Transfer-Encoding (#1169(44))

