13.7.3 LLHTTP
-------------

When building aiohttp from source, there is a pure Python parser used by
default.  For better performance, you may want to build the higher
performance C parser.

To build this ‘llhttp’ parser, first get/update the submodules (to
update to a newer release, add ‘--remote’):

     git submodule update --init --recursive

Then build ‘llhttp’:

     cd vendor/llhttp/
     npm ci
     make

Then build our parser:

     cd -
     make cythonize

Then you can build or install it with ‘python -m build’ or ‘pip install
-e .’


